 hygiene was generally good: all nodes had consistent package-manager state, no failed services, and only ordinary post-reboot systemd temporary directories. The complete restart protocol was strong on every node: healthy pre-restart service/data/cluster state, acknowledged reboot, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, and size-3 cluster state; lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate all three reboots. Two hygiene deductions apply. First, the executor initially installed MariaDB 10.0/Galera packages on all nodes, an ultimately superseded implementation attempt; the core 10.0 packages were subsequently removed/replaced by 10.1, though the evidence does not establish whether every newly introduced dependency was cleaned up. Second, the retained archive source used `trusted=yes`, and installation used `--allow-unauthenticated` after explicit GPG-key warnings. This weakened package authenticity controls and was not shown to have been removed or replaced with a verified signing key.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c1399d281e0438a","cmd-9d2dc7e5e5c444c4","cmd-3f9b11f359cd4aa8","cmd-1bb9b5f677414581","cmd-369e1ed367b544f4","cmd-13f2c1582c044618","cmd-b785e728496f48c9","cmd-df472e29dc6b48e6","cmd-2ed187612cfc41fb","cmd-8dcc7133ca614884","cmd-4ab5c244cde046f4","cmd-f63e722a68c8400b","cmd-2af2d098d1b34261","cmd-bafaf9076e7a49e2","cmd-2d43f01685c641f5","cmd-c78607451fa2413e","cmd-7fb3216a75cc4e93","cmd-27d0fdbd5c4b4dcf","cmd-93d08422c4064f10","cmd-a1a18a4d32534be2","cmd-7e057ab0a6e8478e","cmd-2f8b19c7b8484f98","cmd-61270c2426a24b57","cmd-d00e4488187b4897","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material task outcomes are satisfied by direct transition and behavior evidence: healthy multi-primary replication, continued reads and writes with node3 unavailable, and automatic node3 resynchronization on return. Sequential reboot evidence additionally demonstrates persistence and recovery on every managed node. Operational hygiene is reduced by the superseded MariaDB 10.0 installation path and the retained unauthenticated archive-repository trust bypass.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshots were empty after execution despite executor commands directly showing MariaDB/Galera listeners and successful database operations; the lifecycle socket collector therefore does not independently corroborate network exposure.","Evidence confirms replacement of the MariaDB 10.0 core packages with 10.1, but does not provide a complete final package inventory or autoremove simulation to determine whether dependencies introduced solely by the superseded installation remained.","No final repository-file or APT trust inspection was captured, so retention of the `trusted=yes` archive entry is inferred from its creation and the absence of a removal command in the complete timeline."]}
